(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #103: a function gets its own copy of a thing with a
 text field. Rewriting the parameter's text cannot reach the caller, and
 the only way out is the Return, which copies into the caller's storage.
 A function that falls off its end hands back the all-defaults thing,
 text default included.)

A thing called badge has
  a text called name is "nobody",
  a number called level is 0.

To promoted with a badge called holder.
  Set holder's name to "{holder's name} (senior)".
  Set holder's level to holder's level add 1.
  Return a badge, holder.

To 'maybe badge' with a boolean called 'the choice'.
  a badge called inner.
  Set inner's name to "never seen".
  If 'the choice' then,
    Return a badge, inner.

a badge called worker.
Set worker's name to "Ada".
The boss is promoted of worker.
Print worker.
Print boss.
The chief is promoted of boss.
Print boss.
Print chief.
a badge called unwritten is 'maybe badge' of false.
Print unwritten.
